  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "o4#list-2",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "Side-bar edits write the source",
      "excerpt": "One source edit: the shape the language server already uses, a list of \"replace",
      "text": "we already have a property undo stack and \"nested undo\" where one outer undoable method collapses property changes inside it.  How does that relate?\n\nAlso, what if the editor has not been loaded?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-10-31T04:27:24.832Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "One undo: edits go through the code editor's own model, so typed and side-bar changes share ⌘Z, the unsaved dot and Save. No second undo stack.",
      "offset": 188,
      "edited": "2026-10-31T04:28:19.988Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-10-31T04:43:50.678Z",
          "html": "<p>They fit together well, and your question changed the plan:  the Overview now says the editor keeps its own history, built on the same stack.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>The property undo stack:</b>  it stays the running program's, and side-bar writes never land in it.</li>\n  <li><b>Nested undo:</b>  the editor reuses it, so a drag or an edit to many things is one step.</li>\n  <li><b>Editor not loaded:</b>  the file owns its text, so the edit goes straight into the file, and the unsaved dot and Save still work.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "o8#prose-5",
      "kind": "prose",
      "label": "Code mode that follows along",
      "excerpt": "The maps are line by line for each statement. So following is by statement, not",
      "text": "This is fine",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-10-31T04:32:45.206Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "The maps are line by line for each statement. So following is by statement, not by word, and that's the limit for now",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-10-31T04:32:47.078Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-10-31T04:43:51.428Z",
          "html": "<p>Good, it stays statement by statement.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
